+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Many visitors only want a board for an afternoon, and the desk has to turn them away because rentals are
+priced and accepted by whole days only.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- `addEquipment` accepts an optional `hourlyPrice`: a non-negative integer number of euro cents for one hour.
+- A rental shorter than a day whose `start` and `end` both fall exactly on the hour (UTC) is an hourly rental,
+  priced at the item's `hourlyPrice` multiplied by the number of hours.
+- An item registered without an `hourlyPrice` cannot be rented by the hour: `quote` and `book` throw.
+- Whole-day rentals (midnight to midnight) are unchanged, including the 10% discount from 3 days.
+- Hourly rentals get no discount. Assumption, recorded in the design.
+- Booking an hourly rental uses the same overlap rule as days, so it cannot clash with another booking of the
+  same item.
+
+**In scope:** `addEquipment`, `quote` and `book` for hourly rentals of boards and sails.
+**Out of scope:** lessons, `availability` (it stays whole-day), opening hours, season limits, rentals of a day
+or more that do not start and end at midnight, hourly discounts, cancellation/refunds.
+
+No runtime dependency is introduced.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+- `rentals`: Equipment registration gains `hourlyPrice`; the period requirement admits hourly periods under a
+  day; Quote and Booking price them by the hour.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/index.ts`: the `Equipment` type, `addEquipment` validation, period parsing and `price`.
+- `test/rental.test.ts`: new tests for hourly pricing and rejection cases.
+- Existing behavior and tests for whole-day rentals are unaffected.
